            <profile id="20fb-41ac-6a8e-c2d9" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">The Bearer of the Oriflamme is Stubborn and any unit he leads become Stubborn. The Oriflamme itself can be captured like a banner and if captured (or the bearer is killed) the opponent gets an extra 300 victory points (or 3 ABP if you use Army Break Points). Any Captain may be upgraded to Mercenary Captain (+25) Mercenary Captains are Unreliable and may join a Mercenary unit. Any Mercenary unit within 8” of the Mercenary Captain may use his Leadership vale for all Leadership tests, even though he is a not an army general. The Standard Bearer has a hand weapon and partial plate armour. Army Standard Bearer. May have shield (+1) and full plate armour (+1). May ride a warhorse (+16) that may be cloth barded (+4). May be Stubborn (+3).</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="65a5-47f0-f42a-277e" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="6+">
