            <profile id="ab14-bc3b-d9c1-9460" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapons, thrusting spear, and shield. May have light armour (+2) and may exchange shield for pavise (+1). May exchange thrusting spear for crossbow or handgun (+1). The number of handgunners may not exceed the number of crossbowmen. You may combine Militia with pavise and militia with crossbows into a combined formation. The first rank of crossbowmen can fire at full effect (subsequent ranks cannot fire at all) if the unit is stationary. Crossbowmen not in combined formation are open order. Handgunners are skirmishers. Light Foot</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="c697-4f87-fe72-558b" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
